

## 📄 Production Backend / System Design — Revision Sheet

| Concept                | One-line answer                                                                                     |
| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **DNS**                | Converts a domain name such as `api.civilai.com` into the address of the infrastructure serving it. |
| **HTTP**               | Protocol used for request-response communication between clients and servers.                       |
| **HTTPS**              | HTTP protected by TLS encryption.                                                                   |
| **TLS**                | Provides encryption, integrity, and server authentication for network communication.                |
| **Reverse Proxy**      | Acts as the front door and forwards client requests to internal backend services.                   |
| **Load Balancer**      | Distributes incoming requests across multiple healthy backend instances.                            |
| **Horizontal Scaling** | Handles more traffic by adding more server instances.                                               |
| **Vertical Scaling**   | Handles more traffic by making one server more powerful.                                            |
| **Liveness Check**     | Checks whether a service/process is alive.                                                          |
| **Readiness Check**    | Checks whether a service is actually ready to receive traffic.                                      |
| **JWT**                | A signed credential the client can send so servers can verify the user's identity/claims.           |
| **Stateless JWT Auth** | Each server verifies the JWT without needing to maintain a login session for every request.         |
| **Redis**              | Fast shared storage commonly used for caching, rate limits, sessions, and job brokering.            |
| **Celery**             | Executes background jobs using workers and a message broker such as Redis.                          |
| **Connection Pool**    | Reuses database connections instead of creating a new connection for every request.                 |
| **Service Layer**      | Contains application/business logic.                                                                |
| **Repository Layer**   | Encapsulates database access.                                                                       |
| **PostgreSQL**         | Durable relational database used for persistent application data.                                   |

